.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH check 1  "check " 
.SH NAME
check \- CI\-compatible pass/fail check against policy thresholds
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcheck\fR [\fB\-\-staged\fR] [\fB\-\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIFILE\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
CI\-compatible pass/fail check against policy thresholds
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-staged\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-stdin\fR
Check a supplied diff (e.g. a ref\-range comparison) instead of the working repository. `\-\-path` still selects which `.scrawny.toml` policy applies
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIFILE\fR]
Read the diff from a file instead of stdin
